Managing Multi-Cloud Infrastructure
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Install and configure Ansible for multi-cloud infrastructure management
Write Ansible playbooks to provision resources across AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP)
Configure cloud provider credentials and authentication
Implement dynamic inventories to automatically discover and manage cloud resources
Execute multi-cloud deployment strategies using Infrastructure as Code principles
Troubleshoot common multi-cloud configuration issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of cloud computing concepts (VMs, networks, storage)
Familiarity with YAML syntax and structure
Basic Linux command-line knowledge
Understanding of SSH key pairs and authentication
Knowledge of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) principles
Access to AWS, Azure, and GCP accounts (free tier accounts are sufficient)
Lab Environment
Al Nafi provides Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your dedicated environment. The provided Linux machine is bare metal with no pre-installed tools, so you will install all required software during the lab exercises.

Task 1: Environment Setup and Ansible Installation
Subtask 1.1: Update System and Install Dependencies
First, update your Linux system and install the necessary dependencies:

# Update package repositories
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install Python3 and pip
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip python3-venv git curl unzip -y

# Verify Python installation
python3 --version
pip3 --version
Subtask 1.2: Create Python Virtual Environment
Create an isolated Python environment for Ansible:

# Create a virtual environment
python3 -m venv ansible-env

# Activate the virtual environment
source ansible-env/bin/activate

# Upgrade pip in the virtual environment
pip install --upgrade pip
Subtask 1.3: Install Ansible and Cloud Provider Collections
Install Ansible and the required cloud provider collections:

# Install Ansible
pip install ansible

# Install cloud provider SDK libraries
pip install boto3 botocore azure-cli azure-identity azure-mgmt-compute azure-mgmt-network azure-mgmt-resource google-auth google-cloud-compute

# Install Ansible collections for cloud providers
ansible-galaxy collection install amazon.aws
ansible-galaxy collection install azure.azcollection
ansible-galaxy collection install google.cloud

# Verify Ansible installation
ansible --version
Subtask 1.4: Create Lab Directory Structure
Set up the directory structure for your multi-cloud project:

# Create main project directory
mkdir ~/multi-cloud-lab
cd ~/multi-cloud-lab

# Create subdirectories
mkdir -p {playbooks,inventories,group_vars,host_vars,roles,credentials}

# Create initial files
touch ansible.cfg
touch inventories/hosts.yml
Subtask 1.5: Configure Ansible Settings
Create the Ansible configuration file:

cat > ansible.cfg << 'EOF'
[defaults]
inventory = inventories/hosts.yml
host_key_checking = False
timeout = 30
gathering = smart
fact_caching = memory
stdout_callback = yaml
bin_ansible_callbacks = True

[inventory]
enable_plugins = aws_ec2, azure_rm, gcp_compute

[ssh_connection]
ssh_args = -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=60s
pipelining = True
EOF
Task 2: Configure Cloud Provider Credentials
Subtask 2.1: Set Up AWS Credentials
Configure AWS credentials for Ansible:

# Create AWS credentials directory
mkdir -p ~/.aws

# Create AWS credentials file (replace with your actual credentials)
cat > ~/.aws/credentials << 'EOF'
[default]
aws_access_key_id = YOUR_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
aws_secret_access_key = YOUR_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
EOF

# Create AWS config file
cat > ~/.aws/config << 'EOF'
[default]
region = us-east-1
output = json
EOF

# Set appropriate permissions
chmod 600 ~/.aws/credentials ~/.aws/config
Subtask 2.2: Set Up Azure Credentials
Configure Azure authentication:

# Install Azure CLI (if not already installed)
curl -sL https://aka.ms/InstallAzureCLIDeb | sudo bash

# Login to Azure (this will open a browser for authentication)
az login

# Set your subscription (replace with your subscription ID)
az account set --subscription "YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_ID"

# Create a service principal for Ansible
az ad sp create-for-rbac --name "ansible-sp" --role="Contributor" --scopes="/subscriptions/YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_ID"

# Note down the output values: appId, password, tenant
Create Azure credentials file:

cat > credentials/azure_credentials.yml << 'EOF'
azure_subscription_id: "YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_ID"
azure_client_id: "YOUR_APP_ID"
azure_secret: "YOUR_PASSWORD"
azure_tenant: "YOUR_TENANT_ID"
EOF

chmod 600 credentials/azure_credentials.yml
Subtask 2.3: Set Up GCP Credentials
Configure Google Cloud Platform authentication:

# Download and install Google Cloud SDK
curl https://sdk.cloud.google.com | bash
exec -l $SHELL

# Initialize gcloud
gcloud init

# Create a service account
gcloud iam service-accounts create ansible-sa --display-name="Ansible Service Account"

# Grant necessary permissions
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding YOUR_PROJECT_ID \
    --member="serviceAccount:ansible-sa@YOUR_PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
    --role="roles/compute.admin"

# Create and download service account key
gcloud iam service-accounts keys create ~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/gcp-key.json \
    --iam-account=ansible-sa@YOUR_PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Set environment variable
export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/gcp-key.json
echo 'export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/gcp-key.json' >> ~/.bashrc
Task 3: Create Multi-Cloud Provisioning Playbooks
Subtask 3.1: Create AWS EC2 Instance Playbook
Create a playbook to provision AWS EC2 instances:

cat > playbooks/aws-provision.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Provision AWS EC2 Instance
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  vars:
    aws_region: us-east-1
    instance_type: t2.micro
    ami_id: ami-0c02fb55956c7d316  # Amazon Linux 2
    key_name: ansible-key
    security_group_name: ansible-sg
    
  tasks:
    - name: Create security group
      amazon.aws.ec2_security_group:
        name: "{{ security_group_name }}"
        description: Security group for Ansible managed instances
        region: "{{ aws_region }}"
        rules:
          - proto: tcp
            ports:
              - 22
            cidr_ip: 0.0.0.0/0
            rule_desc: SSH access
          - proto: tcp
            ports:
              - 80
            cidr_ip: 0.0.0.0/0
            rule_desc: HTTP access
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible
      register: security_group

    - name: Create EC2 key pair
      amazon.aws.ec2_key:
        name: "{{ key_name }}"
        region: "{{ aws_region }}"
      register: ec2_key

    - name: Save private key
      copy:
        content: "{{ ec2_key.key.private_key }}"
        dest: "~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/aws-key.pem"
        mode: '0600'
      when: ec2_key.changed

    - name: Launch EC2 instance
      amazon.aws.ec2_instance:
        name: ansible-aws-instance
        image_id: "{{ ami_id }}"
        instance_type: "{{ instance_type }}"
        key_name: "{{ key_name }}"
        security_groups:
          - "{{ security_group_name }}"
        region: "{{ aws_region }}"
        wait: true
        wait_timeout: 300
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible
          Cloud: aws
      register: aws_instance

    - name: Display AWS instance information
      debug:
        msg: 
          - "Instance ID: {{ aws_instance.instances[0].instance_id }}"
          - "Public IP: {{ aws_instance.instances[0].public_ip_address }}"
          - "Private IP: {{ aws_instance.instances[0].private_ip_address }}"
EOF
Subtask 3.2: Create Azure VM Playbook
Create a playbook to provision Azure virtual machines:

cat > playbooks/azure-provision.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Provision Azure Virtual Machine
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  vars_files:
    - ../credentials/azure_credentials.yml
  vars:
    resource_group: ansible-rg
    location: eastus
    vm_name: ansible-azure-vm
    vm_size: Standard_B1s
    admin_username: azureuser
    
  tasks:
    - name: Create resource group
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_resourcegroup:
        name: "{{ resource_group }}"
        location: "{{ location }}"
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible

    - name: Create virtual network
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_virtualnetwork:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        name: "{{ vm_name }}-vnet"
        address_prefixes: "10.0.0.0/16"
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible

    - name: Create subnet
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_subnet:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        name: "{{ vm_name }}-subnet"
        address_prefix: "10.0.1.0/24"
        virtual_network: "{{ vm_name }}-vnet"

    - name: Create public IP
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_publicipaddress:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        allocation_method: Static
        name: "{{ vm_name }}-public-ip"
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible
      register: public_ip

    - name: Create Network Security Group
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_securitygroup:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        name: "{{ vm_name }}-nsg"
        rules:
          - name: SSH
            protocol: Tcp
            destination_port_range: 22
            access: Allow
            priority: 1001
            direction: Inbound
          - name: HTTP
            protocol: Tcp
            destination_port_range: 80
            access: Allow
            priority: 1002
            direction: Inbound
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible

    - name: Create network interface
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_networkinterface:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        name: "{{ vm_name }}-nic"
        virtual_network: "{{ vm_name }}-vnet"
        subnet: "{{ vm_name }}-subnet"
        public_ip_name: "{{ vm_name }}-public-ip"
        security_group: "{{ vm_name }}-nsg"
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible

    - name: Generate SSH key pair
      openssh_keypair:
        path: "~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/azure-key"
        size: 2048
      register: ssh_key

    - name: Create virtual machine
      azure.azcollection.azure_rm_virtualmachine:
        resource_group: "{{ resource_group }}"
        name: "{{ vm_name }}"
        vm_size: "{{ vm_size }}"
        admin_username: "{{ admin_username }}"
        ssh_password_enabled: false
        ssh_public_keys:
          - path: "/home/{{ admin_username }}/.ssh/authorized_keys"
            key_data: "{{ ssh_key.public_key }}"
        network_interfaces: "{{ vm_name }}-nic"
        image:
          offer: 0001-com-ubuntu-server-focal
          publisher: Canonical
          sku: 20_04-lts-gen2
          version: latest
        tags:
          Environment: lab
          ManagedBy: ansible
          Cloud: azure
      register: azure_vm

    - name: Display Azure VM information
      debug:
        msg:
          - "VM Name: {{ azure_vm.ansible_facts.azure_vm.name }}"
          - "Public IP: {{ public_ip.state.ip_address }}"
          - "Resource Group: {{ resource_group }}"
EOF
Subtask 3.3: Create GCP Compute Instance Playbook
Create a playbook to provision GCP compute instances:

cat > playbooks/gcp-provision.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Provision GCP Compute Instance
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  vars:
    project_id: YOUR_PROJECT_ID
    zone: us-central1-a
    region: us-central1
    instance_name: ansible-gcp-instance
    machine_type: e2-micro
    
  tasks:
    - name: Create firewall rule for SSH
      google.cloud.gcp_compute_firewall:
        name: ansible-ssh-firewall
        allowed:
          - ip_protocol: tcp
            ports:
              - '22'
        source_ranges:
          - '0.0.0.0/0'
        target_tags:
          - ansible-managed
        project: "{{ project_id }}"
        auth_kind: serviceaccount
        service_account_file: "{{ ansible_env.GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS }}"
        state: present

    - name: Create firewall rule for HTTP
      google.cloud.gcp_compute_firewall:
        name: ansible-http-firewall
        allowed:
          - ip_protocol: tcp
            ports:
              - '80'
        source_ranges:
          - '0.0.0.0/0'
        target_tags:
          - ansible-managed
        project: "{{ project_id }}"
        auth_kind: serviceaccount
        service_account_file: "{{ ansible_env.GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS }}"
        state: present

    - name: Generate SSH key pair for GCP
      openssh_keypair:
        path: "~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/gcp-key"
        size: 2048
      register: gcp_ssh_key

    - name: Create compute instance
      google.cloud.gcp_compute_instance:
        name: "{{ instance_name }}"
        machine_type: "zones/{{ zone }}/machineTypes/{{ machine_type }}"
        zone: "{{ zone }}"
        project: "{{ project_id }}"
        auth_kind: serviceaccount
        service_account_file: "{{ ansible_env.GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS }}"
        disks:
          - auto_delete: true
            boot: true
            initialize_params:
              source_image: projects/ubuntu-os-cloud/global/images/family/ubuntu-2004-lts
        network_interfaces:
          - access_configs:
              - name: External NAT
                type: ONE_TO_ONE_NAT
        tags:
          items:
            - ansible-managed
        labels:
          environment: lab
          managed-by: ansible
          cloud: gcp
        metadata:
          ssh-keys: "ubuntu:{{ gcp_ssh_key.public_key }}"
        state: present
      register: gcp_instance

    - name: Display GCP instance information
      debug:
        msg:
          - "Instance Name: {{ gcp_instance.name }}"
          - "External IP: {{ gcp_instance.network_interfaces[0].access_configs[0].nat_ip }}"
          - "Internal IP: {{ gcp_instance.network_interfaces[0].network_ip }}"
          - "Zone: {{ gcp_instance.zone }}"
EOF
Subtask 3.4: Create Multi-Cloud Orchestration Playbook
Create a master playbook that orchestrates all cloud deployments:

cat > playbooks/multi-cloud-deploy.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Multi-Cloud Infrastructure Deployment
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  
  tasks:
    - name: Deploy AWS Infrastructure
      include: aws-provision.yml
      tags: aws

    - name: Deploy Azure Infrastructure
      include: azure-provision.yml
      tags: azure

    - name: Deploy GCP Infrastructure
      include: gcp-provision.yml
      tags: gcp

    - name: Wait for all instances to be ready
      pause:
        seconds: 30

    - name: Display deployment summary
      debug:
        msg:
          - "Multi-cloud deployment completed successfully!"
          - "AWS, Azure, and GCP instances have been provisioned."
          - "Use dynamic inventories to manage these resources."
EOF
Task 4: Implement Dynamic Inventories
Subtask 4.1: Create AWS Dynamic Inventory
Create a dynamic inventory configuration for AWS:

cat > inventories/aws_ec2.yml << 'EOF'
---
plugin: amazon.aws.aws_ec2
regions:
  - us-east-1
  - us-west-2
filters:
  tag:ManagedBy: ansible
  instance-state-name: running
keyed_groups:
  - key: tags.Environment
    prefix: env
  - key: tags.Cloud
    prefix: cloud
  - key: instance_type
    prefix: type
hostnames:
  - ip-address
  - dns-name
compose:
  ansible_host: public_ip_address
  ansible_user: ec2-user
  ansible_ssh_private_key_file: ~/multi-cloud-lab/credentials/aws-key.pem
EOF
Subtask 4.2: Create Azure Dynamic Inventory
Create a dynamic inventory configuration for Azure:

cat > inventories/azure_rm.yml << 'EOF'
